id: rtc/battery
_summary: RTC battery tracks the time and ensures the system can wake up from power off state.
_purpose:
 RTC battery backup power can send system wakeup events.
_steps:
 1. Start the test to power off the system (wakeup scheduled in 30s
    unless overridden by RTC_WAKEUP_SECONDS).
_verification:
 RTC can wake up the system successfully.
environ: RTC_DEVICE_FILE RTC_WAKEUP_SECONDS
command: rtc_test.py battery --rtc "${RTC_DEVICE_FILE:-rtc0}" --seconds 30
plugin: user-interact
user: root
category_id: rtc_category
estimated_duration: 40
flags: noreturn

id: rtc/rtc_number
_summary: Check the number of RTC as expected.
_purpose:
    Check the number of RTC on platform as expected.
plugin: shell
user: root
estimated_duration: 1.0
category_id: rtc_category
command: rtc_test.py number
flags: also-after-suspend
environ: TOTAL_RTC_NUM

id: rtc_list
_summary: Generates a RTC list for the platform
_purpose:
 List out all RTC devices on the platform, and generate a list for it.
plugin: resource
user: root
estimated_duration: 1.0
category_id: rtc_category
command: rtc_test.py list

unit: template
template-resource: rtc_list
template-unit: job
id: rtc/rtc_read_{rtc}
template-id: rtc/rtc_read_rtc
_summary: Check that RTC {rtc} can be read
plugin: shell
user: root
category_id: rtc_category
estimated_duration: 5
command: rtc_test.py read --rtc {rtc}
flags: also-after-suspend

unit: template
template-resource: rtc_list
template-unit: job
id: rtc/rtc_alarm_{rtc}
template-id: rtc/rtc_alarm_rtc
depends: rtc/rtc_read_{rtc}
_summary: Check that RTC alarm of {rtc} works
_purpose:
 Set a wakealarm on {rtc} with rtcwake and check that it fires.
 The job command passes --seconds 30 and --timeout 60, which apply to
 every RTC, e.g. "--timeout 60" is equivalent to
 RTC_WAKEUP_TIMEOUT="rtc0:60,rtc1:60,...".
 RTC_WAKEUP_SECONDS and RTC_WAKEUP_TIMEOUT, each a comma-separated list
 of <rtc>:<seconds> entries, override them only for the RTCs they list
 (e.g. RTC_WAKEUP_SECONDS="rtc1:120" and RTC_WAKEUP_TIMEOUT="rtc1:150");
 every other RTC keeps the command values. The timeout must be greater
 than the wakeup time. Devices listed in UNSUPPORTED_RTC_ALARM_DEVICES
 (e.g. "rtc1,rtc2") are skipped.
plugin: shell
user: root
category_id: rtc_category
estimated_duration: 40
environ: UNSUPPORTED_RTC_ALARM_DEVICES RTC_WAKEUP_SECONDS RTC_WAKEUP_TIMEOUT
command: rtc_test.py alarm --rtc {rtc} --seconds 30 --timeout 60
flags: also-after-suspend

unit: template
template-resource: rtc_list
template-unit: job
id: rtc/rtc_clock_{rtc}
template-id: rtc/rtc_clock_rtc
depends: rtc/rtc_read_{rtc}
_summary: Check that {rtc} clock is synchronized with system clock
plugin: shell
user: root
category_id: rtc_category
estimated_duration: 5
environ:
command: rtc_test.py clock --rtc {rtc} --tolerance 5
flags: also-after-suspend
